  "slug": "expanding-glycomics-0644",
  "summary": "New formats and libraries target cohort-scale per-base data and genome-wide regression, while database updates expand underrepresented population variation.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is infrastructure that makes established analyses tractable at cohort or genome scale. pbzarr stores per-base data for thousands of samples in Zarr and is reported to be faster and smaller than D4 and bigWig. RapidGLM, a C++ library with multiple interfaces, is reported to accelerate count-regression differential expression, CRISPR screen and eQTL analyses 2.5-17.8x. A second thread is standardised, programmatic access. pyGENIE wraps AACR GENIE flat files with TMB and mutational signature integration. hlafactor integrates HLA functional annotations (tapasin dependency, expression, NK ligand groups) from two-field genotypes. Met4All packages Infinium methylation array QC through copy-number analysis in a dockerised Shiny app. Resource expansion forms a third strand: CNCB-NGDC adds thirteen new databases, and GI-DB catalogues variation in the underrepresented Indian population. A related public dataset provides haploblock-based genomic hashes for 2,548 1000 Genomes individuals. CATEomics adds model selection and ensembling of CATE estimators for high-dimensional omics.",
